# Copy to mobile/.env. Expo loads it automatically and inlines EXPO_PUBLIC_*
# into the bundle, so a change here needs the dev server restarted.

# Which Speedcubing Central server this build talks to. Overrides app.json's
# extra.apiBaseUrl; see src/lib/config.ts.
#
# Note that 'localhost' is the *phone*, not your development machine, so a real
# device on your own server needs the machine's LAN address
# (e.g. http://192.168.1.20:3001). The Android emulator reaches the host at
# 10.0.2.2.
#
# WCA sign-in is the one feature that does not work against a LAN dev server.
# The app opens WCA with the redirect URI that server is configured with
# (WCA_REDIRECT_URI in the root .env, default http://localhost:3001/...), and
# WCA refuses any redirect URI not registered on the OAuth application:
# "The requested redirect URI is malformed or doesn't match the client redirect
# URI". Only the deployed callback is registered, so point this at the deployed
# origin when testing WCA sign-in. /api/auth/wca/start says so explicitly rather
# than sending you to that WCA error page.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://speedcubingcentral.com
